                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\r\n\r\n**CVE-2024-30171** is a vulnerability identified in the `Portable.BouncyCastle` package version `1.8.9` used in OSS (Open Source Software) projects. This vulnerability arises from improper input validation in cryptographic operations, which could potentially allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service (DoS) by exploiting the flaw in the cryptographic library.\r\n\r\n### General Mitigation Advice\r\n\r\n1. **Upgrade**: The primary mitigation strategy is to upgrade to a patched version of the `Portable.BouncyCastle` package. Check for the latest version and update your dependencies accordingly.\r\n\r\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement strict input validation to ensure that all inputs to cryptographic functions are sanitized and conform to expected formats.\r\n\r\n3. **Code Review**: Conduct a thorough code review focusing on cryptographic operations to identify and rectify any improper handling of inputs.\r\n\r\n4. **Security Patches**: Regularly apply security patches and updates to all dependencies to minimize exposure to known vulnerabilities.\r\n\r\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\r\n\r\nTo address this vulnerability, ensure that all cryptographic operations are performed with validated inputs. Here is a general example of how you might improve input validation in your code:\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\nusing Org.BouncyCastle.Crypto;\r\nusing Org.BouncyCastle.Security;\r\n\r\npublic class SecureCryptoOperations\r\n{\r\n    public void PerformCryptoOperation(byte[] inputData)\r\n    {\r\n        // Validate input data\r\n        if (inputData == null || inputData.Length == 0)\r\n        {\r\n            throw new ArgumentException(\"Input data must not be null or empty\");\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        // Proceed with cryptographic operation\r\n        try\r\n        {\r\n            // Example: Initialize cipher with validated input\r\n            IBufferedCipher cipher = CipherUtilities.GetCipher(\"AES/ECB/PKCS7Padding\");\r\n            // ... (rest of the cryptographic operation)\r\n        }\r\n        catch (CryptoException ex)\r\n        {\r\n            // Handle cryptographic exceptions\r\n            Console.WriteLine(\"Cryptographic operation failed: \" + ex.Message);\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\r\n\r\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\r\n- [OWASP Cryptographic Storage Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html)\r\n\r\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\r\n\r\n- [CWE-20: Improper Input Validation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2024-30171/pkg:nuget/Portable.BouncyCastle@1.8.9"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "glog-2393b626-761e-4ff2-9f69-bb4ba4446d24",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\r\n\r\n**CVE-2020-2934** is a vulnerability found in the `oci/mysql` package, specifically affecting the latest version tagged as `latest`. This vulnerability arises from improper input validation, which can lead to potential SQL injection attacks. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending specially crafted SQL queries, potentially leading to unauthorized access to sensitive data or even complete database compromise.\r\n\r\n### General Mitigation Advice\r\n\r\n1. **Input Validation**: Ensure that all inputs are properly validated and sanitized before being processed by the application. Use parameterized queries or prepared statements to prevent SQL injection.\r\n\r\n2. **Update Dependencies**: Regularly update your dependencies to the latest versions where vulnerabilities are patched. Monitor security advisories for any updates related to the `oci/mysql` package.\r\n\r\n3. **Least Privilege Principle**: Apply the principle of least privilege to database accounts. Ensure that the application uses a database account with the minimum necessary permissions.\r\n\r\n4. **Web Application Firewall (WAF)**: Consider using a WAF to detect and block SQL injection attempts.\r\n\r\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\r\n\r\nTo address this vulnerability, ensure that all SQL queries are parameterized. For example, instead of constructing SQL queries using string concatenation, use prepared statements:\r\n\r\n```go\r\n// Vulnerable code example\r\nquery := \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = '\" + username + \"'\"\r\n\r\n// Recommended fix using parameterized queries\r\nstmt, err := db.Prepare(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ?\")\r\nif err != nil {\r\n    log.Fatal(err)\r\n}\r\ndefer stmt.Close()\r\n\r\nrows, err := stmt.Query(username)\r\nif err != nil {\r\n    log.Fatal(err)\r\n}\r\ndefer rows.Close()\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\r\n\r\n- [OWASP SQL Injection Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://owasp.org/www-project-cheat-sheets/cheatsheets/SQL_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\r\n- [OWASP Top Ten: Injection](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A1_2017-Injection)\r\n\r\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\r\n\r\n- [CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2020-2934/pkg:oci/mysql@latest?tag=latest"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "glog-21d7c8d3-3be9-4dff-addc-92e2bdbf86c8",
