              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\r\nCVE-2024-51417 is a vulnerability identified in the `System.Linq.Dynamic.Core` package, version 1.4.9, used in OSS (Open Source Software) projects. This vulnerability arises from improper input validation in dynamic query execution, which can lead to potential injection attacks. An attacker could exploit this flaw by crafting malicious input that could be executed as part of a dynamic LINQ query, potentially leading to unauthorized data access or manipulation.\r\n\r\n### General Mitigation Advice\r\n1. **Upgrade**: The primary mitigation strategy is to upgrade to a version of `System.Linq.Dynamic.Core` where this vulnerability is patched. Check the official repository or NuGet for the latest secure version.\r\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement strict input validation to ensure that only expected and safe inputs are processed by dynamic queries.\r\n3. **Use Parameterized Queries**: Where possible, use parameterized queries to prevent injection attacks.\r\n4. **Code Review**: Conduct thorough code reviews focusing on areas where dynamic queries are constructed and executed.\r\n\r\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\r\nTo address this vulnerability, consider the following code changes:\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\n// Before: Vulnerable code using dynamic query without validation\r\nvar result = context.Entities.Where(\"Name == @0\", userInput).ToList();\r\n\r\n// After: Secure code with input validation\r\nif (IsValidInput(userInput))\r\n{\r\n    var result = context.Entities.Where(\"Name == @0\", userInput).ToList();\r\n}\r\nelse\r\n{\r\n    // Handle invalid input scenario\r\n    throw new ArgumentException(\"Invalid input provided.\");\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Example of input validation function\r\nbool IsValidInput(string input)\r\n{\r\n    // Implement validation logic, e.g., regex matching, length checks\r\n    return !string.IsNullOrEmpty(input) && input.Length < 100;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\r\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\r\n- [OWASP Injection Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\r\n\r\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\r\n- [CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2024-51417/pkg:nuget/System.Linq.Dynamic.Core@1.4.9"
                ]
              }
