              "id": "glog-0e469065-5588-4f6f-90a3-8b52c875b633",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\r\n**CVE-2024-30172** is a vulnerability identified in the `Portable.BouncyCastle` package version `1.8.9` for the OSS programming language. This vulnerability arises from improper input validation in cryptographic operations, which could potentially allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service (DoS) condition. The issue is particularly critical in environments where the library is used for handling sensitive data or performing cryptographic operations.\r\n\r\n### General Mitigation Advice\r\n1. **Upgrade**: The primary mitigation strategy is to upgrade to a patched version of the `Portable.BouncyCastle` package. Check for newer versions beyond `1.8.9` that address this vulnerability.\r\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement strict input validation to ensure that all data processed by cryptographic functions is sanitized and verified.\r\n3. **Least Privilege**: Run applications with the least privilege necessary to limit the impact of potential exploitation.\r\n4. **Monitoring and Logging**: Implement comprehensive logging and monitoring to detect any unusual activity that might indicate exploitation attempts.\r\n\r\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\r\nIf upgrading is not immediately possible, consider applying the following code-level mitigations:\r\n\r\n- **Validate Inputs**: Ensure that all inputs to cryptographic functions are validated. For example, check the length and format of data before processing.\r\n- **Error Handling**: Implement robust error handling to gracefully manage unexpected inputs or states.\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\n// Example of input validation before cryptographic operations\r\npublic void ProcessData(byte[] inputData)\r\n{\r\n    if (inputData == null || inputData.Length == 0)\r\n    {\r\n        throw new ArgumentException(\"Input data cannot be null or empty\");\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    // Proceed with cryptographic operations\r\n    // ...\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\r\n- [OWASP Cryptographic Storage Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html)\r\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\r\n\r\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\r\n- **CWE-20: Improper Input Validation**: This vulnerability is closely related to CWE-20, which involves the failure to properly validate input data.\r\n\r\nFor more information on CWE-20, visit the [CWE website](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2024-30172/pkg:nuget/Portable.BouncyCastle@1.8.9"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "glog-800f0453-3cf1-4eb9-a3da-c78ba8991419",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\r\n\r\n**CVE-2018-3258** is a vulnerability found in the Oracle MySQL product of Oracle Database Server. This vulnerability affects the MySQL Server component and is related to the Server: Optimizer subcomponent. It allows a low privileged attacker with network access via multiple protocols to compromise MySQL Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in unauthorized ability to cause a hang or frequently repeatable crash (complete DOS) of MySQL Server.\r\n\r\n### General Mitigation Advice\r\n\r\n1. **Update MySQL**: Ensure that you are using the latest version of MySQL, as Oracle regularly releases patches and updates to address known vulnerabilities.\r\n2. **Network Segmentation**: Limit network exposure for MySQL servers. Only allow trusted hosts to connect to the MySQL server.\r\n3. **Access Controls**: Implement strict access controls and ensure that only authorized users have access to the MySQL server.\r\n4. **Monitoring and Logging**: Enable detailed logging and monitoring to detect any unusual activity that could indicate an attempted exploit of this vulnerability.\r\n\r\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\r\n\r\nWhile the specific source code fix for this vulnerability is not publicly available, the general recommendation is to apply the latest patches provided by Oracle. Regularly check for updates and apply them promptly to ensure that your systems are protected against known vulnerabilities.\r\n\r\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\r\n\r\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\r\n- [OWASP Cheat Sheet Series](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/)\r\n\r\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\r\n\r\n- [CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption ('Resource Exhaustion')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html)\r\n\r\nPlease ensure that you regularly review and apply security best practices to protect your systems from known vulnerabilities."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2018-3258/pkg:oci/mysql@latest?tag=latest"
                ]
              }
            },
